WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.020
Like a fairy tale

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.440
It's a sign the story has reached its end

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.360
Like a single passage taken from

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.980
A journey that was too long

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.320
Of the evil that once cast a shadow

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.660
Across this land

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.990
And the memories of the short journey

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.450
With the hero who defeated it

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:29.210
Beyond Journey's End

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.760
The story ends

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.260
And the hero goes to sleep

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.090
Leaving this land with

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.760
Days of peace and quiet

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.270
The passage of time heartlessly

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.430
Makes people forget

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.230
Even the tracks left behind by his life

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.020
Begin to rust

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.860
Just the same

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.150
Your words and wishes and courage

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.490
Are still inside of me

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.360
And they live on

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.910
We chose the same path

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.040
That's all it was supposed to be

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.580
Why is it that at some point

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.830
I wanted to understand the reason for

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.210
The tears that fall down my cheeks

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.290
Even now

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.670
If I retrace the journey we walked together

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.220
Even though you're not there

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:17.890
I know I'll be able to find it

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.480
I see.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.670
I remember now.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.390
It was Frieren.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:46.180
The mage who contributed significantly 
to humanity's analysis of Zoltraak

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:51.080
and slew more demons 
than anyone else in history.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.040
Frieren the Slayer.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.150
One of the geniuses I despise.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.010
Episode 9: Aura the Guillotine

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.190
You'll have to rest for a while.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:16.580
Thank you.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.340
Hey!

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.050
Are you okay?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.170
Because of you, I'll survive.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.640
You have my thanks.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.800
I'll pardon your mage companion as well.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.600
She was right.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.170
Now Frieren can return to town.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.270
Let's have her defeat Lügner 
and the other demon.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:56.000
Ms. Frieren didn't kill the guard.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.040
I know. The demons did it.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:04.710
More importantly, 
that mage's name is Frieren?

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:05.530
Yes.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:09.840
The elven mage who adventured with the Hero?

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.670
Then I've committed a grave discourtesy.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.550
The Granat family owes the 
party of heroes a debt.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:23.370
When this town was attacked by demons 
during my grandfather's rule,

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.440
they were the ones who drove them off.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.810
They faced the same enemy as we do now.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:31.240
It was Aura, one of the 
Seven Sages of Destruction.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.190
It's been a while, Aura.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.180
Indeed, Frieren. About eighty years, I'd say.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.940
You're heading to the town 
up ahead, aren't you?

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.440
I'd appreciate it if you turned back.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.360
No.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.110
Why not?

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.140
Because I have an overwhelming advantage.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.030
Oh?

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.760
You have more puppets than before.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:31.200
Demon magic must be unbelievably 
powerful to control this many.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:35.950
Humanity's magic could never 
dream of reaching such heights.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.720
But your magic couldn't be more disgusting.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:41.790
It makes me want to puke.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.720
That's not a nice thing to say.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.250
It took a lot of work to gather this many.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.890
I recognize some of those suits of armor.

00:05:00.260 --> 00:05:04.310
Aura, it seems I must 
kill you here after all.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:10.540
The Scales of Obedience.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:15.510
It's the reason we haven't been able 
to defeat Aura in all these years.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:22.470
Her magic allows her to force 
others to obey her will.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.540
The magics of the Seven Sages of Destruction

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.970
are beyond human knowledge and reason.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:33.140
Aura places her own soul 
and that of her target on the scales

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.640
and weighs the magnitude of 
their mana against each other.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:40.730
The one with greater mana 
gains control of the other,

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:47.740
turning them into a puppet for all eternity—
until their body withers to dust.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:52.500
It's a risky spell, but that's 
what makes it powerful.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:57.650
And in the hands of someone with mana 
as tremendous as Aura, it's unbeatable.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.910
Is there no way to counter it?

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:06.990
Though the weight of Aura's mana 
is enough to fully tip the scales,

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.970
the scales themselves do judge fairly.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:13.880
If a soul with greater mana than Aura's 
were to be placed on the scales,

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.520
Aura could be defeated.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:24.330
But they say that hasn't happened 
once in the five hundred years

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.520
since Aura became a Sage of Destruction.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:31.020
Then there's no way to fight it?

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.830
There was.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:43.530
Those with powerful wills could 
temporarily resist the spell.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:50.550
The greater the individual, 
the more iron their will.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.680
And even then, it was only temporary?

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.620
But it was a fatal flaw.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.060
The strong-willed must have been 
an obstacle to her.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.550
So...

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:09.690
Aura the Guillotine dealt with them in the 
most logical way after gaining control.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.700
It's a tragic tale.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:23.410
Well? My immortal army 
is powerful, isn't it?

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.300
I'm surprised.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.300
You dispelled the magic I'd cast on them.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.310
No one's ever done that before.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:53.090
Such powerful dispelling magic must expend 
a considerable amount of mana.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.330
Why would you use such a roundabout method?

00:07:58.380 --> 00:08:02.210
The last time we fought, you blew them away 
with flashy spells left and right.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.400
Himmel scolded me afterward.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:12.710
Then that's all the more reason 
not to do this.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.090
Why?

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:17.850
Himmel is long gone, isn't he?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.340
I see. Good.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.300
You demons are monsters after all.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.120
I can kill you without mercy.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:30.820
Okay.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:34.150
I've regained most of my mobility.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:38.730
Father, this place is safe, right?

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.460
Yes. It's not as strong as the 
town's defensive barrier,

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:45.450
but there is a barrier around this church.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:48.160
Then wait here, Graf.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:52.720
Brat, what do you plan to do?

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.890
Do you think the demons will just leave 
if we all hole up in here?

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.000
Mr. Stark, are you serious?

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:04.220
We only landed that hit before 
because we caught him off guard.

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.770
We couldn't find enough of an 
opening to finish him off.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:14.050
If we'd kept fighting, we would 
have been the ones killed.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:18.000
Someone's gotta do this, right?

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:26.580
You're right. Then let's 
do our best together.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.870
No, you go to the guard station.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:34.350
You need to evacuate the townsfolk.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:36.840
Then you're going to...

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.350
Yeah.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:42.990
I'm going to...

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:46.350
get on my hands and knees 
and beg Frieren to return.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:47.940
What?

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:54.340
Come on! Having her defeat him 
is our only option!

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:58.510
I suppose that's more realistic.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.460
The guards will listen to you 
if you show them this.

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.260
Very well.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.130
I'm heading straight out of town.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.380
What is it?

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.270
Your arm is in a terrible state.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.760
Can you pass through the castle gate 
looking like that?

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.800
I'll be fine. This is normal for a warrior.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.220
Is there something weird about it?

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:33.600
I've never seen a warrior walk 
around town with two bloody hands.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:37.600
You're one to talk. You're 
covered in blood, too.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:41.520
Huh? Whose blood is this?

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:43.110
It's not mine.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:49.160
Hey! What's the matter with—

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:55.500
Mr. Stark, there's mana in this blood.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.140
Fern!

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:07.820
An axe?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:16.830
I don't believe it. Am I dreaming?

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.000
That was my master's technique.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:27.250
I'd meant to hit your vitals, 
but then you went and moved.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:30.950
It wasn't my intention to make you suffer.

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.580
Why are you surprised?

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:42.130
Is it because I'm standing here when 
I supposedly suffered a fatal blow?

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:46.130
Or because you didn't detect our approach?

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:54.550
You aren't the only one who knows how to 
conceal her presence by controlling her mana.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:57.640
Any demon can do it.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:05.660
That said, it's hardly fitting 
for a battle between mages.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:08.200
You sure like to talk.

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:10.410
Aren't you going to finish me off?

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:15.960
Since I failed to kill you instantly, 
I thought I'd ask you some questions.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.700
Or would you rather die right now?

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:23.720
Go ahead.

00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.660
Is that boy strong?

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:32.150
He's Eisen the Warrior's best student.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.440
I see. How unfortunate.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:37.800
Poor boy.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:41.230
He won't die a decent death 
at Linie's hands.

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:44.700
One more question.

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.210
Where is Frieren?

00:12:50.090 --> 00:12:51.990
She fled the town

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.290
because you killed the dungeon guard.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.550
Graf Granat said something similar.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:02.260
Killing a guard is a serious crime, it seems.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.220
The punishment is execution.

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:05.550
Execution?

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:09.640
That wouldn't be enough 
to make that woman flee.

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:13.530
She holds a powerful grudge against demons,

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:18.580
enough to teach her own student 
a spell purely for demon-killing.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.650
Someone like that wouldn't run.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.450
She must be after something.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:29.570
It must be Lady Aura.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.460
Don't move.

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:40.280
You know where Ms. Frieren 
is headed, don't you?

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:42.680
You're wasting your time.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:46.880
You lied about failing to kill me.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:51.970
You wanted revenge for my surprising you.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.370
You're proud and arrogant.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:14:01.060
You still don't see us—see anyone 
besides Ms. Frieren as a threat.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:05.160
That's why you granted me an opportunity.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:11.150
From this distance, I can blast 
a hole clean through your heart.

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:13.900
Try it.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.830
Your head will fly before 
you get the chance.

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:29.750
Ms. Frieren, am I useful?

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:31.860
Why would you ask that?

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:37.530
I'm not as good at magic as you are.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:41.820
I've lived for much longer than you.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:44.690
In that regard, you'll never catch up to me.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.070
I see.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.840
But that only applies to mana and technique.

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:57.490
I often let you handle 
battles against monsters.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:00.350
Yes, you've forced those on me many times.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:01.410
I'm sorry, okay?

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:05.700
But battles end quicker when you fight

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:09.200
because you fire off spells 
faster than I do.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:16.980
Girl, I have dedicated the majority 
of my life to the pursuit of magic.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:19.290
So have I.

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:36.450
How is she responding so quickly?

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:41.670
If I hadn't reflexively defended myself, 
that would've pierced my heart.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:43.900
You blocked it.

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.200
So your heart is your weak point.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.710
This girl...

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.210
I see.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:55.460
You weren't lying about 
dedicating your life to magic.

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:59.530
Then I shall crush you with all my might.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.230
Bluterei.

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.800
Sounds like they've begun as well.

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.230
It's a shame, though.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.730
We're nearly finished here.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.020
Perhaps I'll observe their battle.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:20.070
Lord Lügner gets cross when I interfere.

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:26.500
Oh?

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:30.510
We're not finished yet.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:34.260
You're tough. Perhaps I'll be 
able to enjoy this a little.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:42.760
My mana, technique, and control 
are all far greater than hers.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:08.520
This girl cannot compare to me.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:11.510
However, she's fast.

00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:16.090
I'm being overwhelmed by the sheer 
number of attacks, pure and simple.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:27.290
Damn you, Frieren. 
How did you train this girl?

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:34.610
I'll engage her in a battle of attrition 
and wait for her to exhaust her mana.

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:49.130
No, I can't.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:52.580
The battle will be over before then.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:56.190
If I could just create an opening...

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.410
Linie, what are you doing?

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:01.150
Hurry up and defeat him!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.310
Honestly, how selfish.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.070
He's refusing to do anything 
but fight defensively.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:35.210
How are you wielding your axe like that?

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:37.240
Those are my master's techniques.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:40.880
I'm skilled at reading mana.

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:46.360
I memorize the flow of mana 
inside a person when they move

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.450
and imitate their movements.

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:50.140
Just like this.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:17.720
I knew it from the first time I saw 
your movements at the mansion.

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:23.090
They're the same as those of the 
powerful warrior I once memorized.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.040
Coincidences really do happen.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.550
Fate is an interesting thing.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:36.310
You don't mean...

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:40.070
I am imitating the movements 
of Eisen the Warrior.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.050
Seriously? This is crazy.

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:49.360
I can't win this fight.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.320
He finally fell.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.030
I must hurry.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:04.230
Lord Lügner will be upset with me again.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:11.910
"Fell"? Have I fallen?

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:17.560
Stand up, Stark.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:22.540
No matter how battered you get, 
you cannot fall.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:29.890
Yeah, but there's no way I can beat you.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.810
Of course you can't.

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.580
I'm stronger than you.

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:36.630
Then...

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:40.270
But you got back up.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:43.350
That means you haven't lost yet.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.960
What kind of logic is that?

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:50.770
Stark, I'll teach you the secret 
to defeating powerful opponents.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.080
It's simple.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.890
Keep getting back up and hitting them.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:01.740
For warriors, whoever's still standing 
at the end is the winner.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:08.560
Damn it, Master.

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.690
You and your weird logic.

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:14.670
I guess your brain's made of muscles,
 like the rest of you.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.680
You should've just stayed down.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.410
You already lost.

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:24.050
I'm still standing.

00:21:26.190 --> 00:21:28.400
Besides, I remember now.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:30.970
My master's blows were heavier.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.270
Yours are just imitations after all.

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:44.440
Then I will use those imitations 
to send you to your end.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.650
Erfassen.

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:48.560
Bluterei!

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.360
A wide swing, with no regard for defense.

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:04.770
He's lost his mind.

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:16.370
I was prepared for us to kill each other, 
but I shouldn't have been so scared.

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:19.080
Your attacks don't have any 
weight behind them at all.

00:22:21.140 --> 00:22:22.810
Lightning Strike!

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:35.950
Linie!

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:37.160
Shi—

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:38.610
Zoltraak.

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:46.500
Demon-killing magic...

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:52.550
And you alright

00:22:53.060 --> 00:22:55.060
Can you hear me

00:22:55.850 --> 00:23:01.940
Trailing along deserted train tracks

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.270
Crying excessively

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:07.440
Wanting you to smile

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:13.490
I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:17.200
There's something I'd like to tell you

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:19.960
With words more precious than a goodbye

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:25.630
Unremarkable yet special

00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:29.170
See, things that couldn't have been

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:32.220
Seen if it weren't for these eyes

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:36.970
Why? They begin to overflow

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:43.060
So, if I were to be born again

00:23:43.060 --> 00:23:48.900
I would surely choose this place once more

00:23:48.900 --> 00:23:54.910
So, if we were to meet again

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:00.660
I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:03.630
Even if no promises were made

00:24:03.630 --> 00:24:06.550
Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness

00:24:06.550 --> 00:24:12.720
Those tears will be alright, 
dawn will surely break

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:15.390
I'm whispering our lullaby

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:19.310
for you to come back home

00:24:20.130 --> 00:24:21.730
She has roughly one-fifth of my mana.

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:23.130
I've heard there's a long-lived 
mage in these woods.

00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:23.700
If she engages her directly, 
Frieren will lose.

00:24:23.590 --> 00:24:25.760
You are no match for me.

00:24:23.590 --> 00:24:26.230
What do you think, Heiter?

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:25.640
Looks like an elf village.

00:24:25.640 --> 00:24:27.680
Kill all the elves.

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:29.990
Because you're a far more powerful mage.

00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:29.980
Episode 10







A Powerful Mage
